@startuml
title Agent Teams Workflow v2 — delegated approval: grant, claim, and the absent revoke
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

participant "Durable kernel\n(checkpoint)" as kernel #EAF5FF
participant "RSpace run ledger\n(init.rho)" as ledger #CBE7CC
actor "Approver wallet" as approver #FFD8C2
actor "Third party" as other #E7DCF5

kernel -> ledger : advanceRun writes wait_ids + grants\nwaitId|address, one per approver
note over ledger #FFF6C9
A grant is an ACL entry, not a capability:
public string membership, checked against a
chain-derived REV address.
end note

approver -> ledger : claimCommand(approve, waitId, revision)\n(two-phase signed)
ledger -> ledger : re-derive REV address from rho:deploy:data\nmembership: grants.contains(waitId|address)

alt authorized
  ledger -> kernel : resume; kernel counts decisions
  note over kernel #FAD8D8
  Quorum is counted HERE, in the kernel — on
  chain a single grantee can claim. One
  authorized reject resumes regardless of quorum.
  end note
  kernel -> ledger : next advanceRun REPLACES grants wholesale
else unauthorized
  ledger -> approver : abort "command actor is unauthorized"
end

approver -x other : cannot re-delegate\n(the grant names one address)

note over ledger, kernel #FAD8D8
No revoke command exists. A grant ends only
when its wait leaves the ledger at the next
checkpoint — by decision, timeout, cancel, or
migrate. There is no mid-wait revocation.
end note
@enduml
